    "details": {
      "alignment": "Neutral Evil",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "koopa"
      },
      "cr": 3,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Era sheet: 18 Harvestide, 1035 BF, Bowser's Castle.</em> Art and stats describe this figure on the night the castle came down (events.json <code>bowser_throne_room_compromise</code> and <code>the_assault_on_bowsers_castle</code>), not the present day of the campaign (1040 BF).</p><p><strong>Session kit — The Castle Comes Down (Session III).</strong> A GM kit for the night after the breach, not a filed event; nothing on this sheet changes the canon record. The run-sheet is <code>docs/sessions/bowsers-castle-1035-the-castle-comes-down.md</code>.</p><p>The Fawthful record lists Magikoopas in the field beside the defecting Koopa troops. A defected Magikoopa is a loyal one with the sign reversed: the same wand, the same teleport, pointed the other way. Its Block Transport can move Fawthful's soldiers onto a floor Bowser thought was clear — or, worse, move a willing loyalist to the wrong floor and let the routes stop making sense.</p><p>A strip of red cloth on the robe hem is the only tell. DC 10 Wisdom (Perception) to spot which side the wand is on before it fires.</p><p><em>From the record:</em> 'Magikoopas, and defecting Koopa troops in the field.'</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
